<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65130" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάσταξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰκος</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἡ</span> (<i><span class="en">
			Lyc.
			687
		</span></i>), (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μασάομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that with which one chews, mouth, jaws</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ μάστακα χερσὶ πίεζε</span> he
			stopped his <i>mouth</i> with his hands, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.287
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">με . . ἑλὼν ἐπὶ μάστακα
			χερσίν</span> seizing me by the <i>mouth</i>, <i><span class="en">
				23.76
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				144
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμαυρᾶς μάστακος προσφθέγμασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
				</span></i>
			 l. c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάστακι ποππύζων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					5.284.6
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				293.16
			</span></i> (Id.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύσταξ</span>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάσημα</span>
			, <i>mouthful, morsel</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς δ᾽ ὄρνις ἀπτῆσι νεοσσοῖσι
					προφέρῃσι μάστακ᾽, ἐπεί κε λάβῃσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.324
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				753.62
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάστακα δοῖσα τέκνοισιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					14.39
				</span></i>
			; of the olive, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Iamb.</u>
				1.271
			</span></i>; others expl. in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> l. c. as dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάστακι</span>
			<i>in its beak</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάσταξ</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.494d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>locust</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				716
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				802
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Clitarch.
			</span></i> Gloss. ap. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				216.9
			</span></i>. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέστακα</span>.)</div>
